
Ever wanted to make your System-X Pulldown menus white rather than that
ugly red? Well you can, here's how:

1) Install this new version of ibmcon.device

2) Use ibmcon.device for your "Local Display" AND "Display Modes"
   Prefs in SX-Config, using a unit number of 1!!

	eg:

	Display Device:  ibmcon.device            Unit:  1

   Don't forget to set this for every displaymode (ansi, ascii etc)

3) Change your pallete, swap red & white.

   color 0: black
   color 1: white   <--.
   color 2: green      |
     .                 |
     .                 |
     .                 |
   color 7: red     <--'

	Make sure you change this for every palette, "Local Display"
	and "Display Modes". Example .DAT files are included.


  That's it.. You'll get white menus, and perfect ansi.
